PN,11804
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788464144
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G4/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Labour leader Mr Neil Kennock and his
OL,6, wife have been involved in a car crash
OL,7, on their way to Dublin airport.
OL,9,FThey were being driven to the airport
OL,10,Fwhen their driver apparently suffered
OL,11,Fa heart attack, causing their car to
OL,12,Fcollide with a lorry.
OL,14,FThe driver was dead on arrival at the
OL,15,Fcity's Beaumont Hospital.
OL,17,FMr Kinnock was not injured; his wife,
OL,18,FIrish Labour leader Mr Dick Spring and
OL,19,Ftwo Lbbour party staff members also in
OL,20,Fthe car suffered minor injuries. Mr and
OL,21,FMrs Kinnock have resumed their journey.
OL,23,T]CFrom 03-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11805
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788464144
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, South African police have said 58
OL,6, supporters of the Mass Democratic
OL,7, Movement were detained during today's
OL,8, mass beach protest.
OL,9,                   F
OL,10,FThousands of black people defied race
OL,11,Flaws by walking on to Durban's whites-
OL,12,Fonly Addington Beach.
OL,14,FThey picnicked, swam and paddled in the
OL,15,Flatest protest of a campaign leading up
OL,16,Fto Wednesday's whites-only elections.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FRadio South Africa said 10 people were
OL,19,Fstill being held for alleged possession
OL,20,Fof the African National Congress flag.
OL,21,FForty-eight others were released.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 03-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11806
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788464144
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Non-essential personnel were taken off
OL,6, the North-West Hutton oil platform in
OL,7, the North Sea today.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FHelicopters took 113 men to other
OL,10,Fplatforms in the area north-east of
OL,11,FShetland, leaving 75 on board.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FThe evacuation took place after the
OL,14,Fplatform was rocked by a "kick" during
OL,15,Fdrilling, after a high-pressure zone
OL,16,Fwas encountered. No one was hurt.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThe rig's operators, Amoco, have
OL,19,Freported the situation to be under
OL,20,Fcontrol. Production was shut down as
OL,21,Fa precaution following the incident.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 03-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11807
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788464144
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G7/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A former terrorist who received 30
OL,6, life sentences for master-minding an
OL,7, IRA letter-bomb campaign in England
OL,8, has been released from prison.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FShane Paul O'Doherty, who has renounced
OL,11,Fviolence, was released from Maghaberry
OL,12,Fprison near Lisburn in County Antrim
OL,13,Fearlier today.
OL,15,FO'Doherty's release had been expected
OL,16,Ftomorrow but it is thought he may have
OL,17,Fbeen freed early to escape the media.
OL,19,FHe featured in a BBC TV documentary
OL,20,F"Families at War" which was screened
OL,21,Flast month.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 03-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11808
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788464144
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G8/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, TUC General Secrerary Norman Willis
OL,6, has said the tide is running in favour
OL,7, of trade unions.
OL,9,FSpeaking as delegates gathered in
OL,10,FBlackpool for the Trades Union Congress
OL,11,Fwhich begins tomorrow, Mr Willis said
OL,12,Fthe unions were in confident mood.
OL,14,FHe said he was encouraged by recent
OL,15,Fopinion polls showing that more people
OL,16,Fblame management than the unions for
OL,17,FBritain's economic problems.
OL,19,FBut despite this, he said, the unions
OL,20,Fstill felt under attack from the
OL,21,FGovernment and employers.
OL,23,T]CFrom 03-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11809
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788464144
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G9/19
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Former foreign secretary Sir Geoffrey
OL,6, Howe has said he expects to play an
OL,7, active and independent role in his new
OL,8, job as Deputy Prime Minister.
OL,10,FIn an interview on London Weekend
OL,11,FTelevision, Sir Geoffrey dismissed
OL,12,Fsuggestions that he was a "sycophant"
OL,13,Fand said he would be part of a team.
OL,15,FHe did not deny his interest in leading
OL,16,Fthe Conservatives. "I think there is
OL,17,Fnobody who comes into politics who does
OL,18,Fnor cherish that ambition," he said.
OL,19,F
OL,20,FIt was his first major interview since
OL,21,FMrs Thatcher's July Cabinet reshuffle.
OL,23,T]CFrom 03-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
